 ['Woman','The school donated boxes of rock samples, but many labels have fallen off. We cannot put them straight into the teaching collection.'],['Man','Could students identify them as an exercise?'],['Woman','Yes, if we keep those identifications provisional. Some minerals look alike, and a guess should not become a permanent label.'],['Man','The old teacher may have a catalog. I can contact her.'],['Woman','Please do. The boxes have small numbers underneath, so a catalog might reconnect samples with their records. Do not rearrange them yet; their order may help.'],['Man','I will photograph each box as it is and make a separate list of proposed identifications.'],['Woman','That would preserve the current evidence. We can use the uncertain samples for comparison exercises without pretending we already know their names.']
