listen('Why leaves change their angle','talk',[
 ['Speaker','Some plants change the angle of their leaves during a hot day. It is tempting to interpret every such movement as an attempt to catch more sunlight. Yet a leaf can receive more energy than it can safely use. When it turns partly away from the sun, it may reduce heat and water loss rather than maximize light.'],['Speaker','To examine this idea, researchers compared movable leaves with leaves gently held at a fixed angle. They measured surface temperature as well as photosynthesis. Fixed leaves sometimes captured more light but became hotter, especially when soil moisture was low. Movement involved a trade-off: less incoming light could be accompanied by less thermal stress.'],['Speaker','The experiment did not show that one angle was best in all conditions. On a cool morning, facing the sun might be beneficial; during a dry afternoon, the balance could change. The important skill is to connect a visible movement to the conditions under which it occurs, rather than assign it one purpose for the entire day.']
],[
 ['talk','What is the main topic?',['How leaf movement can balance light capture and heat stress','Gerak daun dapat mengurangi panas meski menerima cahaya lebih sedikit.'],[['Why every leaf should face the sun all day','Bacaan menolak satu arah terbaik universal.'],['How to manufacture artificial leaves','Tidak membahas pembuatan daun.'],['Why photosynthesis never requires light','Cahaya tetap sumber energi.']],'Movement involved a trade-off','Dua pengaruh dipertimbangkan bersama.'],
 ['talk','What did the researchers do to some leaves?',['Held them at a fixed angle','Daun ditahan sebagai pembanding daun bergerak.'],[['Removed every leaf from the plants','Tidak ada penghilangan semua daun.'],['Painted them black','Tidak disebut.'],['Kept them underwater','Air tanah dibahas, bukan perendaman daun.']],'leaves gently held at a fixed angle','Perlakuan fisik disebutkan.'],
 ['talk','When did fixed leaves become especially hot?',['When soil moisture was low','Panas meningkat pada kondisi tanah kering.'],[['Only during freezing nights','Bukan malam beku.'],['Whenever the sun disappeared','Hilangnya matahari bukan pemicu yang disebut.'],['Only after every measurement stopped','Pengukuran justru menangkap kondisi itu.']],'especially when soil moisture was low','Kondisi pembatas spesifik.'],
 ['implied','Why might less light sometimes be beneficial?',['It may reduce stress from excess heat','Pengurangan energi masuk mengurangi beban panas.'],[['It guarantees maximum photosynthesis in every case','Ada trade-off, bukan jaminan universal.'],['It prevents all water use by the plant','Water loss berkurang, tidak nol.'],['It makes soil moisture irrelevant','Kelembapan tetap memengaruhi hasil.']],'less incoming light… less thermal stress','Inferensi mengikuti dua pengaruh gerak.'],
 ['intent','What does the speaker recommend when interpreting movement?',['Considering the surrounding conditions','Fungsi berbeda menurut pagi dingin atau sore kering.'],[['Assigning one purpose permanently','Itu justru diperingatkan.'],['Ignoring temperature measurements','Suhu bagian penting bukti.'],['Assuming visible motion has no effect','Efek nyata diuji.']],'connect a visible movement to the conditions','Saran ilmiah utamanya kontekstual.']
]);
listen('A language recorded in letters','talk',[
 ['Speaker','Historical linguists often use private letters to investigate language change. Unlike printed books, letters may preserve informal spellings that suggest how people pronounced words. But a spelling is not a sound recording. Writers can copy conventions learned at school even when their speech differs from them.'],['Speaker','Imagine that a new spelling appears frequently in one town. It might reflect a local pronunciation, but it might also reflect a popular teacher whose students adopted the same written habit. To distinguish these possibilities, a researcher compares writers of different ages and educational backgrounds. Rhymes in local songs may offer another clue, since they depend partly on sound.'],['Speaker','Even a large collection has gaps. People who wrote few letters, or whose papers were not preserved, remain underrepresented. The researcher therefore describes the sample rather than speaking for an entire region without qualification. Letters are valuable because they bring us closer to everyday language, not because they provide unfiltered access to every speaker.']
],[
 ['talk','What is the talk mainly about?',['The usefulness and limits of letters as evidence of past speech','Ejaan informal bisa membantu, tetapi tidak sama dengan rekaman suara.'],[['A method for teaching modern letter writing','Bukan pelajaran menulis surat.'],['Proof that spelling always equals pronunciation','Pembicara membantah hubungan otomatis itu.'],['The invention of sound recording','Rekaman hanya perbandingan.']],'a spelling is not a sound recording','Tema utama adalah batas interpretasi sumber.'],
 ['talk','What alternative explanation is given for a local spelling?',['The influence of a teacher’s writing conventions','Murid mungkin mengadopsi kebiasaan ejaan guru.'],[['A complete absence of schools','Justru pengaruh sekolah dibahas.'],['A law forbidding private letters','Tidak ada larangan.'],['The use of identical voices in recordings','Tidak ada rekaman suara dalam sumber itu.']],'a popular teacher whose students adopted… written habit','Penjelasan alternatif selain pelafalan lokal.'],
 ['talk','Why might local songs be useful?',['Rhymes can provide clues about sounds','Rima bergantung pada bunyi.'],[['They record every person’s education','Tidak memuat riwayat pendidikan semua orang.'],['They guarantee correct letter dates','Tanggal surat tidak ditentukan oleh lagu.'],['They replace the need to compare writers','Perbandingan penulis tetap dibutuhkan.']],'Rhymes… depend partly on sound','Jenis sumber berbeda dapat menambah petunjuk.'],
 ['implied','Why describe the sample carefully?',['Some groups may be missing from the surviving letters','Penulis sedikit surat atau arsip hilang kurang terwakili.'],[['Every resident wrote equally many letters','Tidak semua orang sama banyak menulis.'],['Only printed books can contain language','Letters tetap sumber bahasa.'],['The collection has no useful material','Ada informasi bernilai meski terbatas.']],'remain underrepresented','Cakupan sampel membatasi klaim populasi.'],
 ['paraphrase','“Unfiltered access” would mean',['a direct view without selective influences','Surat tetap disaring kebiasaan tulis dan pelestarian.'],[['a collection stored without cabinets','Bukan filter fisik penyimpanan.'],['a list containing no names','Bukan anonimitas.'],['a recording with a lower volume','Bukan kualitas suara.']],'not because they provide unfiltered access to every speaker','Ungkapan mengkritik anggapan bukti bebas perantara.']
]);
listen('The economics of a spare machine','talk',[
 ['Speaker','A factory considering a spare machine faces a cost that is easy to see and a benefit that is harder to count. The spare may sit unused for months, appearing wasteful. Its value emerges when the main machine fails and production would otherwise stop.'],['Speaker','An analyst compared the purchase cost with records of breakdowns, repair times, and the value of delayed orders. The average expected loss suggested that a spare might pay for itself. However, averages concealed rare but costly failures. Management also had to consider whether a backup could be brought into service quickly; a machine that needed days of installation would not prevent a short interruption.'],['Speaker','The final plan combined a smaller spare with a maintenance contract. This did not eliminate uncertainty. It spread the response across two options: immediate limited production and faster repair of the main equipment. The example shows why an asset can be useful even when it is idle, and why buying a backup is not the same as having a complete recovery plan.']
],[
 ['talk','What is the main issue?',['Evaluating the role of backup equipment','Mesin cadangan bernilai saat mesin utama gagal.'],[['Producing every order twice','Bukan tujuan cadangan.'],['Avoiding all maintenance contracts','Kontrak justru bagian solusi.'],['Keeping the main machine permanently idle','Mesin utama tetap beroperasi normal.']],'Its value emerges when the main machine fails','Topik adalah manfaat kesiapan versus biaya tampak.'],
 ['talk','Which information did the analyst examine?',['Breakdowns, repair times, and delayed orders','Ketiga hal mengukur risiko gangguan.'],[['Only the color of the machines','Warna tidak relevan.'],['The number of factory windows','Tidak disebut.'],['Employees’ favorite products','Preferensi produk bukan sumber analisis.']],'records of breakdowns, repair times, and… delayed orders','Variabel analisis disebut langsung.'],
 ['implied','Why does installation time matter?',['A slow-to-start backup may not prevent a brief stoppage','Cadangan baru berguna bila bisa dipakai tepat waktu.'],[['It determines the machine’s paint color','Tidak terkait.'],['Every repair takes exactly the same time','Waktu bervariasi.'],['A backup never requires setup','Pembicara justru mengingatkan setup.']],'needed days of installation… not prevent a short interruption','Hubungan waktu kesiapan dan durasi gangguan.'],
 ['talk','What did the final plan combine?',['A smaller spare and a maintenance contract','Dua opsi membagi respons gangguan.'],[['Two full-size factories','Tidak membangun dua pabrik.'],['No spare and no repair service','Kebalikannya.'],['Permanent cancellation of all orders','Tidak ada pembatalan demikian.']],'combined a smaller spare with a maintenance contract','Keputusan akhir eksplisit.'],
 ['paraphrase','What does the speaker mean by an idle asset being useful?',['Its readiness can protect against a future interruption','Nilai cadangan tidak hanya pemakaian harian.'],[['Unused machines always increase output directly','Tidak langsung meningkatkan output saat idle.'],['Idle means broken beyond repair','Idle berarti tidak sedang dipakai.'],['Every spare must run continuously','Tidak diperlukan penggunaan kontinu.']],'useful even when it is idle','Parafrasa membedakan fungsi kesiapan dan produksi aktif.']
]);
listen('Layers in a cave wall','talk',[
 ['Speaker','Cave deposits can preserve thin layers that form as mineral-rich water drips from the ceiling. Researchers examine the layers for clues to past rainfall. A thicker layer may suggest faster deposition, but the connection to rainfall is not simple. Water can take different routes through the rock, and changes in soil above the cave can alter the minerals it carries.'],['Speaker','One study compared two formations from the same chamber. Their broad patterns agreed, but a short interval differed sharply. The team did not choose the prettier sequence and ignore the other. They inspected the ceiling and found evidence that a small channel had once redirected water toward one formation.'],['Speaker','The disagreement helped identify a local effect rather than destroy the value of both records. By comparing several deposits and dating them independently, researchers can separate signals shared across a region from those caused by the history of one drip path. A natural archive is most informative when its own formation process is studied alongside the environmental question.']
],[
 ['talk','What is the main topic?',['Interpreting cave layers while considering how they formed','Ketebalan dipengaruhi jalur air dan tanah selain hujan.'],[['Using caves only for tourism','Wisata tidak dibahas.'],['Proving thick layers always mean heavy rainfall','Hubungannya tidak sederhana.'],['Manufacturing minerals in a laboratory','Deposit terbentuk alami.']],'its own formation process is studied','Proses pembentukan perlu dipahami.'],
 ['talk','What can change the minerals in dripping water?',['Changes in the soil above the cave','Tanah di atas gua memengaruhi kandungan mineral.'],[['The color of a researcher’s notebook','Tidak ada hubungan demikian.'],['A ban on independent dating','Penanggalan justru diperlukan.'],['The number of tourists in another country','Tidak disebut.']],'changes in soil above the cave can alter the minerals','Faktor eksplisit dalam paparan.'],
 ['talk','What explained the short disagreement between formations?',['A channel had redirected water toward one of them','Efek lokal pada jalur tetesan.'],[['Both records had been intentionally forged','Tidak ada pemalsuan.'],['The formations came from different planets','Keduanya satu chamber.'],['The researchers forgot to compare any layers','Mereka membandingkan pola secara rinci.']],'a small channel had once redirected water','Pemeriksaan fisik memberi penjelasan.'],
 ['implied','Why compare several deposits?',['To distinguish regional patterns from local effects','Kesamaan lintas lokasi membantu menilai sinyal bersama.'],[['To select only the most attractive one','Pembicara menolak memilih yang prettier.'],['To avoid studying their formation','Proses pembentukan justru diperiksa.'],['To prove water always follows one fixed route','Jalur bisa berubah.']],'separate signals shared across a region','Tujuan perbandingan dinyatakan.'],
 ['intent','How does the speaker treat disagreement in evidence?',['As a clue requiring investigation','Perbedaan membantu menemukan efek lokal.'],[['As a reason to discard every record','Bukan alasan membuang keduanya.'],['As proof that rainfall never changes','Tidak mendukung klaim itu.'],['As a purely aesthetic problem','Bukan soal keindahan pola.']],'The disagreement helped identify a local effect','Perbedaan bisa informatif bila ditelusuri.']
]);
listen('Counting a migrating flock','talk',[
 ['Speaker','Counting birds as they pass a watch station sounds straightforward, but large flocks create several difficulties. Individuals overlap, and the same group may circle back before continuing. A count of visible passages can therefore exceed the number of distinct birds.'],['Speaker','At one coastal station, observers divided the sky into sectors and recorded the direction and time of each flock. When groups returned, the notes helped avoid counting them as entirely new arrivals. Photographs provided another check, although images could miss birds hidden behind others.'],['Speaker','The team reported an estimated range rather than a single exact total. Some readers regarded that as a weakness, but the observers explained that a precise-looking figure would conceal uncertainty that their method could not remove. The range narrowed when several independent observers agreed, and widened during poor visibility. Reporting uncertainty was part of the measurement, not an admission that no useful counting had been done.']
],[
 ['talk','What problem can make passage counts too high?',['The same flock may pass more than once','Kelompok berputar kembali dan dapat terhitung ulang.'],[['All birds stop moving permanently','Burung tetap bermigrasi.'],['No birds overlap in the sky','Tumpang tindih justru masalah lain.'],['Observers record only empty sectors','Mereka merekam flock.']],'the same group may circle back','Satu kelompok tidak selalu satu lintasan.'],
 ['talk','What information helped identify returning groups?',['Their directions and passage times','Catatan waktu dan arah membantu mencocokkan kelompok.'],[['Only the birds’ exact weights','Berat tidak diukur.'],['The names of distant stations','Tidak disebut sumber itu.'],['The age of the cameras','Umur kamera bukan indikator flock.']],'recorded the direction and time of each flock','Rincian metode pencatatan.'],
 ['implied','Why were photographs not a perfect solution?',['Some birds could be hidden behind others','Tumpang tindih masih membatasi gambar.'],[['Photographs cannot show any bird','Bisa dipakai sebagai pemeriksaan tambahan.'],['Every camera was broken','Tidak ada kegagalan semua kamera.'],['The station prohibited images','Foto justru dipakai.']],'images could miss birds hidden behind others','Batas metode tambahan tetap diakui.'],
 ['talk','When did the estimated range become narrower?',['When independent observers agreed','Kesepakatan pengamat memberi ketidakpastian lebih kecil.'],[['Whenever visibility was poor','Visibilitas buruk memperlebar rentang.'],['When all notes were discarded','Catatan dipertahankan.'],['When a single observer guessed without checking','Bukan kesepakatan independen.']],'range narrowed when several independent observers agreed','Kondisi penyempitan rentang disebutkan.'],
 ['paraphrase','What does reporting a range communicate?',['The useful estimate includes acknowledged uncertainty','Rentang bukan berarti tidak ada pengukuran berguna.'],[['The team counted no birds at all','Penghitungan nyata dilakukan.'],['The exact total is known without doubt','Rentang justru mengakui ketidakpastian.'],['Every number inside it was directly observed as a separate population','Rentang bukan beberapa populasi berbeda.']],'Reporting uncertainty was part of the measurement','Makna akhir menjaga kegunaan dan kejujuran hasil.']
]);
